<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves up to $1.94 bln at April 4.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves up to $1.94 bln at April 4.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.94 billion on April 4, up $27 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In March, international reserves grew $139 million.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of 1996, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
